    q: 'What is membranous nephropathy?',
    a: 'Membranous nephropathy is an autoimmune kidney disease in which antibodies attack the filtration barrier of the glomerulus, so protein spills into the urine (often at nephrotic range). It is one of the classic causes of nephrotic syndrome in adults.',
  },
