  {
    q: 'How is this different from giving ACTH?',
    a: 'ACTH activates MC2R and raises cortisol, and it also hits other melanocortin receptors. Resomelagon is built to drive the MC1R/MC3R resolution arm (ERK1/2) while largely sparing cAMP-linked pigment signalling and ignoring MC2R — the same therapeutic idea without the stress-hormone lever.',
